/*
remoteEnv
---------

Key–value pairs that set or override environment variables **only** for the JetBrains IDE
backend and its helper processes (such as integrated terminals), **not** for the entire
Docker container.

• Values can reference host-side or predefined variables.
• Choose **remoteEnv** over **containerEnv** when the variable needs to change at runtime
  because remoteEnv can be updated without rebuilding the whole container (once
  rebuild/restart logic is fully in place).

-------------------------------------------------
containerEnv vs. remoteEnv (at a glance)
-------------------------------------------------
containerEnv – Baked into the image during `docker build`; visible to every process
               in the container; changes require a rebuild.

remoteEnv    – Injected when the JetBrains IDE backend starts; affects only the
               backend and its sub-processes; can be refreshed on restart.

Default guideline: use **containerEnv** unless you specifically need the flexibility
of runtime updates provided by **remoteEnv**.
*/

{
  "name": "1_4-spec_remoteEnv",
  "image": "ubuntu:latest",
  "remoteEnv": {
    "DYNAMIC_VAR": "initial"
  },
  "containerEnv": {
    "STATIC_VAR": "initial"
  }
}
